Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 09 41 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS on excisional biopsy  comedo type                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  PREDOMINATELY GRADE 1 WITH FOCAL GRADE 2  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AND LOCATED FAR AWAY FROM MARGINS  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 15 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  3  ONE INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  4  COMPLEX SCLEROSING LESION  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  6  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The metastatic deposits in the lymph node aggregate to  0 1cm and consist of cohesive  whorled epithelial cell clusters located in the subcapsular sinuses  Their epithelial nature is confirmed by positive cytokeratin immunostaining  The slightly spindled morphology of the cells and the nuclear atypia are histologically similar to areas of the patient s ductal carcinoma in situ  Despite extensive examination and thorough sampling of the mastectomy specimen  no invasive carcinoma is found in the breast parenchyma itself  Review of the patient s prior biopsy specimens does not reveal any invasive component  Drs  Dennis Sgroi and Ben Pilch have reviewed selected slides and concur with the diagnosis of metastatic carcinoma  The ductal carcinoma in situ demonstrates a prominent spindle cell morphology in many areas  and there is also focal comedonecrosis  A Grimelius stain is negative for argyrophilic granules  Stains for ER  PR  and Her 2 neu will be attempted on the remaining lymph node tissue and will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 57                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block O   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  No tumor cells are seen in the section stained for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 26 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm tan pink nipple bearing skin ellipse and a 9 x 6 x 2cm axillary tail marked by a suture  On the tan pink skin surface there are two linear scars  one in the upper inner quadrant measuring 2 8cm in greatest dimension  and a second scar in the lower inner quadrant measuring 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two well healing biopsy cavities which are adjacent to each other  located in the medial aspect of the breast  The more medial of the cavities measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  The adjacent biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The cavities are surrounded by fat necrosis  The more medial of the cavities is 0 6cm to the closest posterior margin while the other cavity is 2cm to the closest posterior margin  The remainder of the breast is notable for diffuse thick fibrous tissue with numerous cysts ranging in size from 0 2cm to 1 4cm  Additionally there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm pink papillary nodule in the midline of the breast which is located 2cm from the closest posterior margin  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes  which range in size from REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 9cm to 0 2cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE A B  Biopsy cavity  1  with closest posterior margin in A  C D  Biopsy cavity  2  E  Small papillary mass  F  Fibrocystic change from lower inner quadrant  G  Fibrocystic change and posterior margin from lower outer quadrant  H  Fibrocystic area from upper inner quadrant  I  Fibrocystic change from upper outer quadrant  J  Axillary lymph node  bisected and entirely submitted  K P  Axillary lymph nodes  entirely submitted  Q R  Representative sections of largest lymph node  S Z  Biopsy cavities  AA BB  Remainder of largest lymph node  CC    axillary lymph node  DD HH  Parenchyma JJ KK  Biopsy cavity LL  Parenchyma Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unknown.
