le  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oval tan pink cavity with a rubbery wall  The cavity is located 0 7cm from the posterior deep margin  1 8cm from the overlying retract skin and 2 5cm from the anterior soft tissue margin  The cavity lining is tan pink  smooth and glistening  The borders are tan pink  rubbery and fibrotic with focal tan yellow areas  consistent with fat necrosis  The surrounding uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow to pink unremarkable fibroadipose with no satellite lesions identified  Within the possible attached axillary tail a few possible tan pink lymph nodes are identified ranging form REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Cavity to overlying posterior margin  C J  Entire cavity with surrounding parenchyma  K L  Uninvolved parenchyma  M  4 whole possible lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node  1  740   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of tan yellow to pink lobulated unoriented fibroadipose tissue containing 5 tan pink lymph nodes ranging from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in maximum dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  N  1 bisected lymph node  O  1 whole lymph node  P  1 bisected lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node  2  200   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregular tan yellow to pink lobulated unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue containing one possible tan pink lymph node which is submitted in cassette Q  The remaining parenchyma is sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes R W  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm of irregular tan pink lobulated portions of fibroadipose tissue and a few overlying tan pink irregular unremarkable portions of skin  The specimen weighs 150 grams in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan yellow to pink fibroadipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted are submitted in cassettes X GG  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  Brian Ian Labow  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA  740  EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA  200  EXCISION PART D  BREAST LEFT  MAMMOPLASTY , Unknown.
